; EGTools++ — module-definition file.
;
; Exports the Excel XLL entry points with UNDECORATED names.
;
; On x86, __stdcall symbols are name-decorated by the compiler
; (xlAutoOpen -> _xlAutoOpen@0). Excel's Add-in Manager looks up the *plain*
; names via GetProcAddress, so without this .def `RegisterXLL` fails on 32-bit
; Excel (the entry point is invisible). x64 has no such decoration, which is why
; the 64-bit build loaded while the 32-bit one did not (O2 finding, 2026-06-27,
; verified against Excel 2016 32-bit). See plan/11_x86_로드버그_수정.md.
;
; The symbols themselves are provided by the statically-linked xlOil-XLL.lib;
; this file only renames their exports. Mirrors xlOil's own
; src/xlOil-Loader/xlOilAddin.def (plus xlAddInManagerInfo12 for the manager
; display name, which is compiled in and confirmed present).
EXPORTS
	xlAutoOpen
	xlAutoClose
	xlAutoFree12
	xlAddInManagerInfo12
	xlHandleCalculationCancelled
